Decoder states:
    The decoder can be in one of these states:

    Open:
        Ready to receive and interpret data, actively processing incoming signals or information from connected sources.

    Closed:
        Not receiving or interpreting data and possibly unable to proceed with normal operations.

    The decoder always starts in the open state.

Encoder states:
    Similar to the decoder but for outgoing data.
